exports[`export snapshots on the sample flawed Run (ROADMAP 14.3, SPEC §4.10.4) > SPEC-EXP-01: fixPrompt of the flawed Run is stable and names every failing or needs-review requirement 1`] = `
"You are fixing a web page so it matches its design. Page: "Sample landing page", URL: https://sample.test/flawed/.
Viewports checked: Desktop 1440 px, Mobile 390 px. Contract version 1, run 2023-11-14.
Fix ONLY the items below. Leave everything that already passes unchanged.

1. [Critical · Desktop · Explicit] R-01 Nothing is drawn where the design shows content: The hero shows an illustration at the right of the headline (ink 76.1% in the design vs 0.3% in the implementation), measured from images.
   Observed: Ink coverage: 0.3% (capture image) vs 76.1% (design image).
   Suggested fix: Add the missing element at the position shown in the design.
   Done when: An illustration of about 520 x 400 px is visible at the right of the hero at 1440 px.

2. [Major · Desktop · Explicit] R-02 Primary CTA is 132 px wide vs 220 px in the design (−40.0%), measured from DOM snapshot.
   Observed: Primary CTA width: 132 px (DOM snapshot) vs 220 px (design image), -40%.
   Element: body &gt; main:nth-of-type(1) &gt; section:nth-of-type(1) &gt; div:nth-of-type(1) &gt; a:nth-of-type(1)
   Suggested fix: Make \`body &gt; main:nth-of-type(1) &gt; section:nth-of-type(1) &gt; div:nth-of-type(1) &gt; a:nth-of-type(1)\` 220 px width (or match the design's width rule) at a 1440 px viewport.
   Done when: The Start free button width is within tolerance of 220 px at 1440 px.

3. [Major · Desktop · Explicit] R-03 The headline "Plan your week, calmly" is 28 px, smaller than other text at 32 px, so it is not the dominant text; measured from DOM snapshot.
   Observed: The headline "Plan your week, calmly" font size vs the largest other text: 28 px (DOM snapshot) vs 32 px (DOM snapshot).
   Element: body &gt; main:nth-of-type(1) &gt; section:nth-of-type(1) &gt; div:nth-of-type(1) &gt; h1:nth-of-type(1)
   Suggested fix: Make \`body &gt; main:nth-of-type(1) &gt; section:nth-of-type(1) &gt; div:nth-of-type(1) &gt; h1:nth-of-type(1)\` larger than every other text on the page (more than 32 px).
   Done when: The h1 font size is at least that of every other text element at 1440 px.

4. [Major · Desktop · Explicit] R-04 The navigation contains four links: found 3 visible matching elements, expected 4, measured from DOM snapshot.
   Observed: Matching elements: 3 (DOM snapshot) vs 4 (contract).
   Suggested fix: Render exactly 4 of these elements.
   Done when: The nav landmark holds exactly 4 links at 1440 px.

5. [Major · Desktop · Explicit · verify first] R-07 The call-to-action uses the design colour and the arrow icon: this could not be confirmed, so check it by eye. The button hue looks close to the design, but the icon looks like a chevron instead of an arrow.
   Observed: no measurement recorded, verify against the design.
   Suggested fix: Use the design arrow icon and the design button colour.
   Done when: The Start free button has the same colour as the design and an arrow icon, not a chevron.

6. [Minor · Desktop · Explicit] R-06 The vertical gap is 64 px vs 96 px in the design (−33.3%), measured from DOM snapshot.
   Observed: vertical gap: 64 px (DOM snapshot) vs 96 px (design image), -33.3%.
   Element: #features &gt; h2:nth-of-type(1)
   Suggested fix: Set the space between \`body &gt; main:nth-of-type(1) &gt; section:nth-of-type(1)\` and \`#features &gt; h2:nth-of-type(1)\` to 96 px.
   Done when: The vertical gap from the hero to the features heading is within tolerance of 96 px.

7. [Minor · Mobile · Inferred] I-M-01 Expected the mobile page to fit the screen without overlap (inferred). The page does not fit its viewport: 64 px of horizontal overflow; 15 overlapping pairs (Main over Plan your week, calmly A simple planner…, and more), measured from DOM snapshot. (inferred)
   Observed: Horizontal overflow: 64 px (DOM snapshot) vs 0 px (contract); Overlapping pairs: 15 (DOM snapshot) vs 0 (contract); Clipped text elements: 0 (DOM snapshot) vs 0 (contract).
   Element: body &gt; nav:nth-of-type(1)
   Suggested fix: Remove the horizontal overflow, separate the overlapping elements and stop clipping text at 390 px.
   Done when: At 390 px there is no horizontal scroll and no overlapping or clipped text.

Inferred items are advisory: no design shows that viewport.
After fixing, take new screenshots and DOM snapshots at the same widths so the result can be re-verified.
"
`;

